= 25 July 1974 — Geneva opens amid continued fighting

Mert Zorlu described what he had seen in those days, during the ceasefire, as follows:

“They brought us down from Ankara in a day and left us on the island by helicopter on 22 July. There was continual fighting. The Beşparmak Mountains were swarming with Greek Cypriot and Greek soldiers. Throughout the ceasefire this situation continued. Whenever fire came from somewhere, we immediately advanced and took the hill... The Greek soldiers in particular were big, giant-like men. They fought fiercely, but the Greek Cypriots immediately ran away...”

Mehmet Ali Birand, 30 Sıcak Gün, PDF page 272–273 — English translation of the source excerpt.


- @historical: Continue consolidating positions while opening the Geneva talks.
- @alternative: Freeze offensive movement and seek UN-monitored protection and supply arrangements.

